  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Total federal contract obligations in North Dakota are $629M for FY2026 to date. Award activity in the state so far includes 2,041 awards with an average award size of $308K, and obligations are down 23.4% year over year. The Department of Health and Human Services is the largest buyer, obligating $275M, followed by the Department of Defense at $167M and the Department of Transportation at $86.1M. Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the largest industry by obligations at $219M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction next at $115M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the largest vendor, receiving $256M in obligations, while WALSH FEDERAL LLC follows at $74.4M. Fiscal-year comparisons show FY26 obligations at $629M versus prior annual totals of $780M in FY21, $973M in FY22, $803M in FY23, $980M in FY24, and $821M in FY25. This snapshot covers partial current-year totals; FY2026 to date amounts will change as the fiscal year progresses.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How has federal contracting in North Dakota trended recently?",
        "body": "Year-over-year obligations in North Dakota are down 23.4% in FY2026 to date. Fiscal-year totals show FY26 at $629M versus $821M in FY25 and $980M in FY24, with earlier years at $803M for FY23, $973M for FY22, and $780M for FY21. Award count and average award size for FY2026 to date are 2,041 awards and $308K respectively."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, vendors, and industries dominate FY2026 to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Health and Human Services leads buying activity at $275M, followed by the Department of Defense at $167M and the Department of Transportation at $86.1M. NORIDIAN HEALTHCARE SOLUTIONS, LLC is the top vendor with $256M in obligations, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers is the top industry at $219M, with Commercial and Institutional Building Construction at $115M."
      }
    ]
  },
